1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,305
Glycolysis, in thirty seconds.

2
00:00:02,755 --> 00:00:06,297
It happens in the cytoplasm, and it does not need oxygen.

3
00:00:06,547 --> 00:00:11,645
One glucose, with six carbons, is split into two pyruvate, with three carbons each.

4
00:00:12,095 --> 00:00:14,122
Here's the part exams like to test.

5
00:00:14,372 --> 00:00:20,815
It spends two ATP early on and makes four, so the net gain is two ATP, plus two NADH.

